# Sprint 3 Retrospective

**Project:** Migrant Hub — student onboarding and blogging platform
**Sprint:** Sprint 3 (17 September – 7 October 2026)
**Team:** Pratham Arora, Yun Wang, Prabhleen Kaur, Sajib Das, Sehwinder Singh
**Scrum Master:** Sajib Das
**Format:** 4Ls

## Liked

- We agreed on the API contract early, so the frontend and backend matched when
  we finally joined them.
- Everyone had their own part and knew what to do. The task split was written
  down at the start of the sprint and we worked to it.
- The AI feature still lets you publish even when it does not answer. We built
  the failure path on purpose instead of hoping the service would be up.

## Learned

- How to test an API with Vitest and Supertest, including routes that need a
  token.
- How login and tokens work from start to finish: hashing the password, issuing
  the token, verifying it, and checking that a post belongs to the person
  editing it.
- Gemini returned 503 on most of our attempts near the deadline because the free model was busy.

## Lacked

- We did not say who owns which file. Two of us rewrote the same file on the
  same night and had to resolve it by hand afterwards.
- We left the documents part until the end. 

## Longed for

- Joining the frontend and backend earlier than the final week.
- Time to put the site online.


## Workload distribution

The work was split in the Sprint 3 task split document: three members on the
frontend and two on the backend, with roughly equal numbers of tasks each. The
Sprint 2 retrospective said the work had not been even, so this sprint we agreed
the split in writing before any code was written.

Commit counts are not even across the team, because some work was paired, some
was pushed from one machine and documentation and design do not appear as
commits. What each person owned is recorded in the task split document.

## Communication

We met over Zoom and used WhatsApp daily. Attendance was full at
every meeting. When somebody was stuck, another member stopped and helped rather
than leaving it to the next day.

## Metrics

- Sprint 3 backlog: 44 items planned.
- Completed: All of the tasks items on the board.
- Not completed: deployment. It was named in our sprint goal and is carried
  forward rather than dropped.
- Velocity: Sprint 2 was 25 of 26 items. Sprint 3 was 45 of 45.
- Team satisfaction: We are all satisfied with our work this sprint.
- Attendance: full at every meeting.


